Wanted/problem: Buyers are not merely asking for a good digital likeness.
They expect the approved representation to survive the transition into the
delivered medium. A preview that looks right can actually increase
disappointment if the manufactured/printed result changes face geometry,
crop, placement, color or sharpness.

Current workaround/product: sellers provide a digital/model preview before
production, but production itself can introduce a second failure surface.

Roast.pet implication: Treat PRINT PROOF as distinct from PET IDENTITY
PROOF. The identity image/video can be approved first; once mapped onto the
actual card/shirt/product, show a final production-representative
mock/proof with exact crop, QR placement, text safe area and resolution
checks. For initial QR cards, this can be automated and nearly free.

